Subject: [PATCH 23/61] NNS.ARMA: forecast a constant series with a numeric
 seasonal.factor

With a numeric seasonal.factor the lag weights are based on the ratio of
each lag's CV to the series CV. For a constant series both are 0/0, the
weights were NaN and every forecast was NaN. Use equal weights when the
computed weights are not finite. (The auto-seasonality path of a
constant series was fixed by the zero-weight fallback in the previous
commit.)

Before -> after:
  NNS.ARMA(rep(5, 60), h = 3, seasonal.factor = 12)          NaN NaN NaN -> 5 5 5
  same, method = "lin"                                        NaN NaN NaN -> 5 5 5
  seasonal.factor = c(12,24), all four methods               NaN -> 5 5 5
  NNS.ARMA(rep(-2, 30), h = 2, seasonal.factor = 7)          -> -2 -2
Non-constant series are unchanged.
---
 R/ARMA.R | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/R/ARMA.R b/R/ARMA.R
index d1151ef..96e76d8 100644
--- a/R/ARMA.R
+++ b/R/ARMA.R
@@ -121,6 +121,9 @@ NNS.ARMA <- function(variable,
       Seasonal.weighting <- 1 / pmax(Relative.seasonal, .Machine$double.eps)
       Observation.weighting <- 1 / sqrt(seasonal.factor)
       Weights <- (Seasonal.weighting * Observation.weighting) / sum(Observation.weighting * Seasonal.weighting)
+      # A constant series has CV 0/0 = NaN for every lag: weight the lags equally
+      # instead of propagating NaN into the forecast.
+      if(any(!is.finite(Weights))) Weights <- rep(1/length(lag), length(lag))
       seasonal.plot <- FALSE
     } else {
       Weights <- weights
